ACCEPTANCE / LIMITS
The before tests fail at the synchronous production-dispatch seam; the after tests pass through real GUI/Logic/PTY controls while the fixture provider remains held. No second record loader or DTO and no production custody in the fixture. The bounded concurrency/cancellation tests prove a cancelled waiter cannot create unlimited blocking jobs. The source and records above are a handoff, pending Oracle verification.
The cap is documented in the spec and here. The LocalTab host note is complete and read by Nyx; Settings/document hosting was not implemented.
No --parity, --slow, ignored Keychain tests, 967-seat run or large-corpus throughput benchmark was run for this non-paint change. The 22 default ignores and 8 named slow skips remain named in the logs. No desktop driving, code signing or peer process/target cleanup. Cancellation does not hard-stop synchronous provider IO; its permit remains occupied until it returns. Copy-on-write catalogue update cost under a very large concurrent corpus was not measured. Seat MCP knowledge calls and R5g's checkpoint-specific serial-link scheduling are outside this change.

